{
  "convention": "All times in seconds. 'open_start_s', 'vanilla_close_start_s' are measured relative to the MOUNT LINE (log line '[utpp_vehicle_anim] ride N: workspot animVariables') in door-timeline.json of the car-door game test of 2026-11-01. The entry clip frame 0 plays 'clip_start_after_mount_s' after the mount line (measured 0.010..0.040 s). OFFLINE MODEL: the door-open event E (the instant the door starts to move) is at mount line + open_start_s = clip time open_start_s - clip_start_after_mount_s; 'close_after_s' (per seat clip) = seconds from E to the start of the door close; vanilla close_after = vanilla_close_start_s - open_start_s (about 1.51 s swing doors, 1.80 s Turbo-R). The offline model maps the startup/recover clips of the vehicle linearly onto open_dur_s / close_dur_s (measured: first to last movement frame). GAME (redscript utpp_vehicle_door.reds): the close is scheduled from the OnVehicleDoorOpen event with the event's own vanilla autoCloseTime, NOT from the detected door motion (some doors start moving ~0.05 s after the event), so the shipped number is only the extra delay: UTPPCarDoorCloseDeltaS(seat variable) = max over the female / male clip of (close_after_s - vanilla_close_after_s of the class / door side), clamped at >= 0 and rounded up to the ms (generated utpp_vehicle_door_timing.reds; -1.0 = seat without UTPP timing); redscript closeAfter = evt.autoCloseTime + delta, applied only when delta > 0. Both numbers share the event anchor, so the anchor cancels. The shipped close the offline gate must clear is vanilla_close_after_s + delta (check_door_clearance.py --table --close-from-timing).",
  "clip_start_after_mount_s": 0.025,
  "window_s": 0.02,
  "v_lag_s": 0.3,
  "v_lag_set_s": [
    0.0,
    0.15,
    0.3
  ],
  "v_lag_note": "UNVERIFIED safety allowance, not a measurement: V's body is evaluated v_lag_s LATER than the clip clock (frame 0 held for that long). Reason: with zero lag the closing sweep at the measured vanilla close time clears most installed (pk-door2) clips, but the 2026-11-01 review saw the door close on V's shoulder/head/arm/knee at 1.6-1.9 s; a lag scan (check_door_clearance.py --v-lag) reproduces those failures at 0.2 s (standard2, standard25/3/utility passenger), 0.3 s (standard25/3 driver) and 0.4 s (sport1). The real offset between the mount line and V's motion in the game has not been measured to this precision.",
